# Next.js Frontend Conventions

## Stack & Version Notes

- Next.js 16 + React 19 — APIs may differ from older Next.js versions
- App Router with route groups: `(auth)` for login/register, `(dashboard)` for protected pages
- Tailwind CSS 4 with custom utility classes in `globals.css` (`.btn`, `.card`, `.input`, `.modal-overlay`)

## File Organization

```
src/app/          → pages and layouts (App Router)
src/lib/axios.ts  → single API client (always use this, not raw fetch)
src/types/        → TypeScript interfaces matching API DTOs
src/providers/    → React context (AuthProvider)
```

## Client vs Server Components

- Pages with hooks, localStorage, or event handlers → `'use client'` at top
- Root `layout.tsx` wraps children in `AuthProvider`
- Auth guard logic lives in `AuthProvider` — do not duplicate redirect logic in pages

## API Integration

- Base URL is `/api/v1` (proxied to backend via `API_PROXY_TARGET` env var)
- Controller routes are singular: `/expense`, `/category`, `/auth`, `/reports`, `/export`
- JWT attached automatically by axios interceptor from `localStorage`
- 401 responses redirect to `/login` when no valid token
- Blob downloads: `api.get('/export/csv', { responseType: 'blob' })`

## UI Patterns

- Use `lucide-react` for icons
- Dark mode enabled via `className="dark"` on `<html>`
- Admin-only nav items: check `user.role?.toLowerCase() === 'admin'`
- Keep types in sync with backend DTOs in `src/types/index.ts`

## Environment

`.env.local` needs `API_PROXY_TARGET=https://localhost:{api-port}` (no trailing slash)
